# InterMUN Intentional UI Rule

Designs should feel premium, calm, and human — with **one clear font system**.

## Typography (strict)
- **UI everywhere** (body, headings, buttons, nav, marketing, auth): **Inter**
- Hierarchy = size + weight only (`400` body · `600` subheads · `700` titles)
- **Documents only** (resolutions / papers): Merriweather via `.font-serif`
- Dyslexic mode: OpenDyslexic (with Atkinson Hyperlegible fallback)
- Do **not** mix Instrument Serif, Clash Display, cursive scripts, or Inter Tight into product UI
- Avoid Poppins + Inter + Manrope stacks

## Color & Tone
- Background base: pastel blue `#DFF2FC` with soft wash to `#EDF8FF` / `#F8FBFF`
- Ink: `#183148` · secondary `#35516B` · muted `#4D6174` (≥4.5:1)
- Navy CTAs: `#17324A` · accent fill `#119ED3` · readable accent text `--accent-text`
- Borders: `#C9DDE9`

## Layout & Composition
- Auth / gates: split navy brand panel + white form (desktop)
- Prefer asymmetry / staggered sections; intentional whitespace
- Never clone identical section structures back-to-back

## Buttons & Microcopy
- Primary = navy filled; secondary = soft bordered
- Descriptive CTAs; conversational copy

## Constraints
- Keep existing component naming/IA intact
- Enhance only via color, texture, motion — do not change labels or structural naming
